Today is Saturday morning.
I wake up early.
I take Asha's dog, Moti, for a walk in the nearby park.
Asha's rule is very clear.
Moti must always be kept on the leash in the park.
Leaving him loose is strictly forbidden.
The weather is very nice and we walk on the grass.
Moti is very happy.
Suddenly, he sees a squirrel.
The squirrel is near a big tree.
Moti barks loudly.
He wants to run after the squirrel.
He pulls the leash hard.
I hold the leash tightly.
I say to him, "Moti, stop!"
"Don't catch it!"
"Come here and sit near me."
Moti stops and looks at me.
I pet him.
I say, "Very good, Moti."
